nto a blob, so a further figure there cannot be wholly excluded. Read as 28.1.25 on the pattern of the identically stamped 27125 on sw740gd4329. Region 5 is the printed leader label (Welte-Mignon No. 10, The harmonious Blacksmith, Handel)."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/hx184ww0780.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":1.7554,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/hx184ww0780.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/hx184ww0780.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"AVG_HOLE_WIDTH of the roll's SUPRA analysis: the parser's box at its own grey level, averaged over every perforation it kept, so that a tear or a run of dust drags it. On the three copies measured both ways, an edge at half the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/h/hx184ww0780_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"chainPitch":{"value":2.5093,"unit":"mm","slot":1.8777,"bridge":0.633,"n":441,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/hx184ww0780.jsonld#chain-pitch-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/hx184ww0780.jsonld#chain-pitch-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"Median over 441 pitches of held notes, measured on the IIIF image by punch-225/dates/pitch.py; slot and bridge are medians of their own.","used":["https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/hx184ww0780%2Fhx184ww0780_0001/","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"advance":{"value":0.496,"unit":"mm","strength":0.4085,"n":22329,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/hx184ww0780.jsonld#advance-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/hx184ww0780.jsonld