he date and is illegible to me; it may begin Hoff-. The day's second figure is an 8 written as two strokes converging on a single bottom bowl, so the upper loop is open; 6 can be ruled out because two strokes descend into the bowl. A three-figure group, perhaps 134, preceded by a letter, follows the date; I could not read it with confidence and have left roll_number empty."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/jn782fq7439.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":2.2858,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/jn782fq7439.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/jn782fq7439.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"AVG_HOLE_WIDTH of the roll's SUPRA analysis: the parser's box at its own grey level, averaged over every perforation it kept, so that a tear or a run of dust drags it. On the three copies measured both ways, an edge at half the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/j/jn782fq7439_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"chainPitch":{"value":3.0834,"unit":"mm","slot":2.5224,"bridge":0.5369,"n":317,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/jn782fq7439.jsonld#chain-pitch-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/jn782fq7439.jsonld#chain-pitch-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"Median over 317 pitches of held notes, measured on the IIIF image by punch-225/dates/pitch.py; slot and bridge are medians of their own.","used":["https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/jn782fq7439%2Fjn782fq7439_0001/","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"advance":{"value":1.066,"unit":"mm","strength":0.1278,