17,101157,460,1900/full/90/default.jpg","transcription":{"@type":"text","@id":"copies/gq990gn6753.jsonld#inscription-text","text":"141?23"},"medium":"pencil"}]}],"scan":"https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/gq990gn6753%2Fgq990gn6753_0001/","readFrom":{"kind":"scan"},"production":{"company":{"name":"M. Welte & Söhne","sameAs":[]},"system":{"@id":"https://w3id.org/reo/type/system/welte-t100"},"date":{"after":"1923-01-01","before":"1923-12-31","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/gq990gn6753.jsonld#date-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/gq990gn6753.jsonld#date-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"meaningComprehension","comprehends":["copies/gq990gn6753.jsonld#inscription-text"],"note":"Pencil, read from the lower (180-degree) panel. A run of figures without separators, written close to the edge of the paper. The closing 2 and 3 are plain, so the year is 1923, and the run opens with a narrow 1 followed by a figure with a closed head, most likely 14 though 19 is possible. Between them stand two upright strokes joined by a short bar at mid height, which read either as a single open 4 (14.4.23) or as two figures, 11 (14.11.23) or 17 (no month). I cannot settle the middle group from this scan, so only the year is recorded. The roll number comes from region 2, which carries 375 alone, the 7 there crossed and carried on a long top bar."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/gq990gn6753.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":1.7731,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/gq990gn6753.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/gq990gn6753.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"AVG_HOLE_WIDTH of the roll's SUPRA analysis: the parser's box at its own grey level, averaged over every perforation it kept, so that a tear or a run of dust drags it. On the three copies measured both ways, an edge at half the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/g/gq990gn6753_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"chainPitch":{"value":2.4961,"unit":"mm","slot":1.8473,"bridge":0.6506,"n":225,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/gq990gn6753.jsonld#chain-pitch-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/gq990gn6753.jsonld#chain-pitch-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"Median over 225 pitches of held notes, measured on the IIIF image by punch-225/dates/pitch.py; slot and bridge are medians of their own.","used":["https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/gq990gn6753%2Fgq990gn6753_0001/","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"advance":{"value":0.496,"unit":"mm","strength":0.4449,"n":5154,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/gq990gn6753.jsonld#advance-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/gq990gn6753.jsonld#advance-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"The strongest period the 5154 slot lengths keep, by punch-225/advance.py (punch-225/dates/step.py); runners-up 0.412 mm at 0.0686, 0.608 mm at 0.0938. The chain pitch is 5.032 of it. Held likely when found at a strength of at least 0.35 with the pitch within 0.15 of a whole number of it, possible when one of the two holds, unlikely when neither does.","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/g/gq990gn6753_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/step.py"]}]}}}}}}},{"@type":"RollCopy","@id":"copies/sr504pc8797.jsonld#copy","label":"Condon Roll 122","identifier":"Stanford Libraries CONDON ROLL 122","seeAlso":"https://purl.stanford.edu/sr504pc8797"