ut. Here the UPPER panel is the upright one. Day, month and the first three figures of the year are plain. The last figure I read as a 7: its right-hand stroke rises above the small loop and comes down as the bar and diagonal of a 7, unlike the plainly round-bowled 9 two places earlier. 1909 cannot be entirely excluded."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/sr504pc8797.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":1.9838,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/sr504pc8797.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/sr504pc8797.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"AVG_HOLE_WIDTH of the roll's SUPRA analysis: the parser's box at its own grey level, averaged over every perforation it kept, so that a tear or a run of dust drags it. On the three copies measured both ways, an edge at half the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/s/sr504pc8797_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"chainPitch":{"value":2.8082,"unit":"mm","slot":1.9825,"bridge":0.8187,"n":521,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/sr504pc8797.jsonld#chain-pitch-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/sr504pc8797.jsonld#chain-pitch-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"Median over 521 pitches of held notes, measured on the IIIF image by punch-225/dates/pitch.py; slot and bridge are medians of their own.","used":["https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/sr504pc8797%2Fsr504pc8797_0001/","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"advance":{"value":1.376,"unit":"mm","strength":0.2351,"n":19521,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/sr504pc8797.jso