eft open."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/hs635sh6729.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":1.807,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/hs635sh6729.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/hs635sh6729.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"AVG_HOLE_WIDTH of the roll's SUPRA analysis: the parser's box at its own grey level, averaged over every perforation it kept, so that a tear or a run of dust drags it. On the three copies measured both ways, an edge at half the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/h/hs635sh6729_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"chainPitch":{"value":2.6008,"unit":"mm","slot":1.9186,"bridge":0.6694,"n":413,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/hs635sh6729.jsonld#chain-pitch-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/hs635sh6729.jsonld#chain-pitch-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"Median over 413 pitches of held notes, measured on the IIIF image by punch-225/dates/pitch.py; slot and bridge are medians of their own.","used":["https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/hs635sh6729%2Fhs635sh6729_0001/","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"advance":{"value":0.518,"unit":"mm","strength":0.5887,"n":12970,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/hs635sh6729.jsonld#advance-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/hs635sh6729.jsonld#advance-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"The strongest period the 12970 slot lengths keep, by punch-225/advance.py (punch-225/dates/step.py); runners-up 0.422 mm at 0.0742, 0.662 mm at 0.0725