-serif numeral type; here the UPPER panel is the upright one. The four figures are perfectly clear, the 2 filled in with ink, and two faint marks stand a little to the right of the 5, perhaps the remains of a further stamped character. Read as the usual run without separators, 7 1 25 gives 7 January 1925, which fits the corpus. What I cannot show from the image is that the group is a date at all rather than a roll or serial number, and there is no hand or separator to corroborate it, so the confidence is low for that reason and not because of any figure. Region 2 carries no writing."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/yg667ds7662.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":1.7072,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/yg667ds7662.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/yg667ds7662.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"AVG_HOLE_WIDTH of the roll's SUPRA analysis: the parser's box at its own grey level, averaged over every perforation it kept, so that a tear or a run of dust drags it. On the three copies measured both ways, an edge at half the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/y/yg667ds7662_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"chainPitch":{"value":2.5157,"unit":"mm","slot":1.7861,"bridge":0.7324,"n":324,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/yg667ds7662.jsonld#chain-pitch-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/yg667ds7662.jsonld#chain-pitch-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"Median over 324 pitches of held notes, measured on the IIIF image by punch-225/dates/pitch.py; slot and bridge are medians of their own.","used":["https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iii