w484ky7093.jsonld#chain-pitch-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"Median over 261 pitches of held notes, measured on the IIIF image by punch-225/dates/pitch.py; slot and bridge are medians of their own.","used":["https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/yw484ky7093%2Fyw484ky7093_0001/","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"advance":{"value":0.491,"unit":"mm","strength":0.3573,"n":4805,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/yw484ky7093.jsonld#advance-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/yw484ky7093.jsonld#advance-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"The strongest period the 4805 slot lengths keep, by punch-225/advance.py (punch-225/dates/step.py); runners-up 0.388 mm at 0.0603, 0.635 mm at 0.1143. The chain pitch is 6.086 of it. Held likely when found at a strength of at least 0.35 with the pitch within 0.15 of a whole number of it, possible when one of the two holds, unlikely when neither does.","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/y/yw484ky7093_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/step.py"]}]}}}}}}},{"@type":"RollCopy","@id":"copies/xm978sg7252.jsonld#copy","label":"Condon Roll 222","identifier":"Stanford Libraries CONDON ROLL 222","seeAlso":"https://purl.stanford.edu/xm978sg7252","exemplifies":{"catalogueNumber":"WM 592","label":"Galston, Gottfried (1879-1950): Waltzes op. 39, no. 15 and 16"},"keeper":{"name":"Stanford University Libraries","sameAs":[]},"conditions":[],"measurements":{"scanResolution":{"value":300.25,"unit":"px/in"},"holeSeparation":{"value":3.199,"unit":"mm"}},"modifications":[{"@type":"Alteration","purpose":"control","produced":[{"@type":"Writing","@id":"copies/xm978sg7252.jsonld#inscription","technique":"handwriting","horizontal":{"unit":"mm","from":10750.31,"to":10911.04},"vertical":{"unit":"track","from":90,"to":103},"depiction":"https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/xm978sg7252%2Fxm978sg7252_0001/3513,127078,460,1900/full/90/default.jpg","transcription":{"@type":"text","@id":"copies/xm978sg7252.jsonld#inscription-text","text":"91824  (e4 separately: 592)"}}]}],"scan":"https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/xm978sg7252%2Fxm978sg7252_0001/","readFrom":{"kind":"scan"},"production":{"company":{"name":"M. Welte & Söhne","sameAs":[]},"system":{"@id":"https://w3id.org/reo/type/system/welte-t100"},"date":{"after":"1924-01-01","before":"1924-12-31","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/xm978sg7252.jsonld#date-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/xm978sg7252.jsonld#date-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"meaningComprehension","comprehends":["copies/xm978sg7252.jsonld#inscription-text"],"note":"Five pencil figures in e2, written right at the paper edge, with the top of every figure sheared off by that edge even in the extended crop; the lower halves are clear. Read 9 1 8 2 4. The first figure is built exactly like the 9 of the 592 written in e4 (closed oval with the stroke descending to the lower left), not like that hand's 2, which has a flat base to the right. The closing 2 matches the hand's 2; the last figure I take for a 4 from its lower half only. How to group them I cannot settle from the image: 9-18-24 (month first) gives 18 September 1924, while a 2 in place of the 9 would allow 21.8.24 or 2-18-24. The roll is a Welte-Mignon no. 592 with an English label (Brahms waltzes, played by G. Galston, e5), so I cannot assume the German day-first order here. Year 1924 is the part I would stand behind; the day and month I have deliberately left out. e1, e3 blank; e6 colour target."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/xm978sg7252.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":1.7579,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/xm978sg7252.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/xm978sg7252.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"AVG_HOLE_WIDTH of the roll's SUPRA analysis: the parser's box at its own grey level, averaged over every perforation it kept, so that a tear or a run of dust drags it. On the three copies measured both ways, an edge at half the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/x/xm978sg7252_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"chainPitch":{"value":2.5102,"unit":"mm","slot":1.886,"bridge":0.6196,"n":155,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/xm978sg7252.jsonld#chain-pitch-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/xm978sg7252.jsonld#chain-pitch-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"Median over 155 pitches of held notes, measured on the IIIF image by punch-225/dates/pitch.py; slot and bridge are medians of their own.","used":["https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/xm978sg7252%2Fxm978sg7252_0001/","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"advance":{"value":0.497,"unit":"mm","strength":0.4423,"n":8105,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/xm978sg7252.jsonld#advance-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/xm978sg7252.jsonld#advance-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"The strongest period the 8105 slot lengths keep, by punch-225/advance.py (punch-225/dates/step.py); runners-up 0.408 mm at 0.0546, 0.821 mm at 0.0535. The chain pitch is 5.051 of it. Held likely when found at a strength of at least 0.35 with the pitch within 0.15 of a whole number of it, possible when one of the two holds, unlikely when neither does.","used":["https://raw.github