8 mm at 0.048, 0.644 mm at 0.0906. The chain pitch is 3.117 of it. Held likely when found at a strength of at least 0.35 with the pitch within 0.15 of a whole number of it, possible when one of the two holds, unlikely when neither does.","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/q/qq244fh1388_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/step.py"]}]}}}}}}},{"@type":"RollCopy","@id":"copies/qw257qp8232.jsonld#copy","label":"Condon Roll 232","identifier":"Stanford Libraries CONDON ROLL 232","seeAlso":"https://purl.stanford.edu/qw257qp8232","exemplifies":{"catalogueNumber":"WM 690","label":"Neitzel, Otto (1852-1920): Symphonische Etüde"},"keeper":{"name":"Stanford University Libraries","sameAs":[]},"conditions":[],"measurements":{"scanResolution":{"value":300.25,"unit":"px/in"},"holeSeparation":{"value":3.19,"unit":"mm"}},"modifications":[{"@type":"Alteration","purpose":"control","produced":[{"@type":"Writing","@id":"copies/qw257qp8232.jsonld#inscription","technique":"handwriting","horizontal":{"unit":"mm","from":44349.2,"to":44509.94},"vertical":{"unit":"track","from":82,"to":98},"depiction":"https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/qw257qp8232%2Fqw257qp8232_0001/3246,524246,540,1900/full/90/default.jpg","transcription":{"@type":"text","@id":"copies/qw257qp8232.jsonld#inscription-text","text":"[slug mark] - 5 6 2 8   (e2, in pencil: 690)"}}]}],"scan":"https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/qw257qp8232%2Fqw257qp8232_0001/","readFrom":{"kind":"scan"},"production":{"company":{"name":"M. Welte & Söhne","sameAs":[]},"system":{"@id":"https://w3id.org/reo/type/system/welte-t100"},"date":{"within":"1928-06-05","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/qw257qp8232.jsonld#date-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/qw257qp8232.jsonld#date-belief","certainty":"true","reasons":[{"@type":"meaningComprehension","comprehends":["copies/qw257qp8232.jsonld#inscription-text"],"note":"Stamped across the roll in e1, reading along the paper: a heavy fixed mark of stacked bars, a hyphen, then 5 6 2 8, all four figures cleanly inked. The mark is the slug's own, not a digit - the figures alone already give a possible date, so I have not let it make the day 15. Day first gives 5 June 1928. e2 carries 690 in pencil, and the leader label in e3 reads 'WELTE-MIGNON No. 690, Symphonische Etude, Schumann, Gespielt von' with Otto Neitzel's signature, M. Welte & Söhne, Freiburg i. Br., so the roll number is certain and the hand is the German workshop's."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/qw257qp8232.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":1.763,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/qw257qp8232.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/qw257qp8232.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"AVG_HOLE_WIDTH of the roll's SUPRA analysis: the parser's box at its own grey level, averaged over every perforation it kept, so that a tear or a run of dust drags it. On the three copies measured both ways, an edge at half the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/q/qw257qp8232_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"chainPitch":{"value":2.5064,"unit":"mm","slot":1.884,"bridge":0.6224,"n":411,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/qw257qp8232.jsonld#chain-pitch-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/qw257qp8232.jsonld#chain-pitch-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"Median over 411 pitches of held notes, measured on the IIIF image by punch-225/dates/pitch.py; slot and bridge are medians of their own.","used":["https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/qw25