,"note":"Read as \"Fritz\". The ornate F, unmistakable beside roll 225's; the reader recorded it as an illegible name."},{"@type":"inference","premises":[],"used":["https://pfefferniels.github.io/condon-dates/hands.jsonld"],"note":"The signature is clustered with the hand's other rolls by comparing the inscription images, not by the name read."}]}}}}],"scan":"https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/qg121rz6125%2Fqg121rz6125_0001/","readFrom":{"kind":"scan"},"production":{"company":{"name":"M. Welte & Söhne","sameAs":[]},"system":{"@id":"https://w3id.org/reo/type/system/welte-t100"},"date":{"after":"1909-01-01","before":"1909-12-31","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/qg121rz6125.jsonld#date-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/qg121rz6125.jsonld#date-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"meaningComprehension","comprehends":["copies/qg121rz6125.jsonld#inscription-text"],"note":"Faint pencil in a Kurrent hand on paper ruled with the scanner's lines, which cross the writing. Five tokens: the number 1259, a word of five or six letters with a long bar over the middle of it, the day 10, a four-letter word, and the year 09 with a full stop. The number, the day and the year are firm. The month is written out rather than in figures and I cannot read it: its letter pattern is tall, short, tall, short, which fits Febr as well as Juli, and the initial is a looped ascender with a descender that could be either F or J. The name after the number is likewise beyond me; the bar over it is the Kurrent mark for a doubled m or n. I give the year alone in date_iso rather than guess a month."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/qg121rz6125.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":2.2723,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/qg121rz6125.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/qg121rz6125.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"AVG_HOLE_WIDTH of the roll's SUPRA analysis: the parser's box at its own grey level, averaged over every perforation it kept, so that a tear or a run of dust drags it. On the three copies measured both ways, an edge at half the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/q/qg121rz6125_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"chainPitch":{"value":3.0144,"unit":"mm","slot":2.4067,"bridge":0.6131,"n":275,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/qg121rz6125.jsonld#chain-pitch-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/qg121rz6125.jsonld#chain-pitch-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"Median over 275 pitches of held notes, measured on the IIIF image by punch-225/dates/pitch.py; slot and bridge are medians of their own.","used":["https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/qg121rz6125%2Fqg121rz6125_0001/","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"advance":{"value":1.01,"unit":"mm","strength":0.8539,"n":13747,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/qg121rz6125.jsonld#advance-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/qg121rz6125.jsonld#advance-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"The strongest period the 13747 slot lengths keep, by punch-225/advance.py (punch-225/dates/step.py); runners-up 0.338 mm at 0.2871, 0.506 mm at 0.5659. The chain pitch is 2.985 of it. Held likely when found at a strength of at least 0.35 with the pitch within 0.15 of a whole number of it, possible when one of the two holds, unlikely when neither does.","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/q/qg121rz6125_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2