ps://pfefferniels.github.io/condon-dates/hands.jsonld"],"note":"The signature is clustered with the hand's other rolls by comparing the inscription images, not by the name read."}]}}}}],"scan":"https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/gs573tj9547%2Fgs573tj9547_0001/","readFrom":{"kind":"scan"},"production":{"company":{"name":"M. Welte & Söhne","sameAs":[]},"system":{"@id":"https://w3id.org/reo/type/system/welte-t100"},"date":{"within":"1912-01-29","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/gs573tj9547.jsonld#date-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/gs573tj9547.jsonld#date-belief","certainty":"true","reasons":[{"@type":"meaningComprehension","comprehends":["copies/gs573tj9547.jsonld#inscription-text"],"note":"Ink, upper panel upright: the number at the left, the date in the middle, one name to the right and a second below it. Every figure of the date is plain. Wössler is the hand already known from this corpus; the name above it I read as Hohmüller, though the minims after Hohm- could as well give Hohmüler and I cannot be sure of the umlaut."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/gs573tj9547.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":2.3585,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/gs573tj9547.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/gs573tj9547.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"AVG_HOLE_WIDTH of the roll's SUPRA analysis: the parser's box at its own grey level, averaged over every perforation it kept, so that a tear or a run of dust drags it. On the three copies measured both ways, an edge at half the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/g/gs573tj9547_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"chainPitc