ark, crop 4 a row of small pencil loops drawn round particular perforations, which look like a repairer's or inspector's marks rather than writing, and crop 5 the paper end."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/nq190zp1066.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":1.8027,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/nq190zp1066.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/nq190zp1066.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"AVG_HOLE_WIDTH of the roll's SUPRA analysis: the parser's box at its own grey level, averaged over every perforation it kept, so that a tear or a run of dust drags it. On the three copies measured both ways, an edge at half the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/n/nq190zp1066_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"chainPitch":{"value":2.5064,"unit":"mm","slot":1.9526,"bridge":0.5627,"n":255,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/nq190zp1066.jsonld#chain-pitch-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/nq190zp1066.jsonld#chain-pitch-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"Median over 255 pitches of held notes, measured on the IIIF image by punch-225/dates/pitch.py; slot and bridge are medians of their own.","used":["https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/nq190zp1066%2Fnq190zp1066_0001/","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"advance":{"value":0.494,"unit":"mm","strength":0.2659,"n":22980,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/nq190zp1066.jsonld#advance-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/nq190zp1066.jsonld#advance-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"meas