ld be read 5, giving 1546 instead of 1346; and the initials at the end are three letters closed by a point, whose capital could be H or K, so Hst. is the best I can make of them."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/xx912rs1788.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":2.1411,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/xx912rs1788.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/xx912rs1788.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"AVG_HOLE_WIDTH of the roll's SUPRA analysis: the parser's box at its own grey level, averaged over every perforation it kept, so that a tear or a run of dust drags it. On the three copies measured both ways, an edge at half the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/x/xx912rs1788_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"chainPitch":{"value":3.067,"unit":"mm","slot":2.2422,"bridge":0.8167,"n":444,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/xx912rs1788.jsonld#chain-pitch-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/xx912rs1788.jsonld#chain-pitch-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"Median over 444 pitches of held notes, measured on the IIIF image by punch-225/dates/pitch.py; slot and bridge are medians of their own.","used":["https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/xx912rs1788%2Fxx912rs1788_0001/","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"advance":{"value":0.508,"unit":"mm","strength":0.4435,"n":33878,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/xx912rs1788.jsonld#advance-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/xx912rs1788.jsonld#advance-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"me