trast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/f/fz215xr4723_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"chainPitch":{"value":2.605,"unit":"mm","slot":1.8587,"bridge":0.7353,"n":410,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/fz215xr4723.jsonld#chain-pitch-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/fz215xr4723.jsonld#chain-pitch-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"Median over 410 pitches of held notes, measured on the IIIF image by punch-225/dates/pitch.py; slot and bridge are medians of their own.","used":["https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/fz215xr4723%2Ffz215xr4723_0001/","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"advance":{"value":0.522,"unit":"mm","strength":0.6268,"n":35106,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/fz215xr4723.jsonld#advance-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/fz215xr4723.jsonld#advance-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"The strongest period the 35106 slot lengths keep, by punch-225/advance.py (punch-225/dates/step.py); runners-up 0.344 mm at 0.0187, 0.69 mm at 0.0636. The chain pitch is 4.990 of it. Held likely when found at a strength of at least 0.35 with the pitch within 0.15 of a whole number of it, possible when one of the two holds, unlikely when neither does.","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/f/fz215xr4723_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/step.py"]}]}}}}}}},{"@type":"RollCopy","@id":"copies/kg488qt3887.jsonld#copy","label":"Condon Roll 453","identifier":"Stanford Libraries CONDON ROLL 453","seeAlso":"https://purl.stanford.edu/kg488qt3887","exemplifies":{"catalogueNumber":"WM 1447","label":"Schelling, Ernest (1876-1939): 2 préludes : op. 28, Nr. 1, C-Dur u. Nr. 21, B-Dur"},"keeper":{"name":"Stanford University Libraries","sameAs":[]},"conditions":[],"measurements":{"scanResolution":{"value":300.25,"unit":"px/in"},"holeSeparation":{"value":3.205,"unit":"mm"}},"modifications":[{"@type":"Alteration","purpose":"control","produced":[{"@type":"Writing","@id":"copies/kg488qt3887.jsonld#inscription","technique":"handwriting","horizontal":{"unit":"mm","from":14985.37,"to":15146.1},"vertical":{"unit":"track","from":89,"to":102},"depiction":"https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/kg488qt3887%2Fkg488qt3887_0001/3497,177140,460,1900/full/90/default.jpg","transcription":{"@type":"text","@id":"copies/kg488qt3887.jsonld#inscription-text","text":"1447  6 5 09  [short name, not read]"},"medium":"pencil"}]}],"scan":"https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/kg488qt3887%2Fkg488qt3887_0001/","readFrom":{"kind":"scan"},"production":{"company":{"name":"M. Welte & Söhne","sameAs":[]},"system":{"@id":"https://w3id.org/reo/type/system/welte-t100"},"date":{"within":"1909-05-06","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/kg488qt3887.jsonld#date-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/kg488qt3887.jsonld#date-belief","certainty":"true","reasons":[{"@type":"meaningComprehension","comprehends":["copies/kg488qt3887.jsonld#inscription-text"],"note":"pencil, upper panel upright, no separators between the date figures. The 6 has a single bowl and a curved ascender, the 5 is the two-stroke form with its top bar written separately, and 09 is plain. In the roll number the fourth figure is not shaped like the leading 1: it reads most nearly as 7, though 9 cannot be excluded. A short surname follows the date, apparently beginning May- and ending in three minims; I could not read it with confidence."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/kg488qt3887.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"valu