sons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"The strongest period the 8029 slot lengths keep, by punch-225/advance.py (punch-225/dates/step.py); runners-up 0.406 mm at 0.1212, 0.632 mm at 0.1595. The chain pitch is 5.044 of it. Held likely when found at a strength of at least 0.35 with the pitch within 0.15 of a whole number of it, possible when one of the two holds, unlikely when neither does.","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/v/vz717bq6543_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/step.py"]}]}}}}}}},{"@type":"RollCopy","@id":"copies/pv279zy5193.jsonld#copy","label":"Condon Roll 492","identifier":"Stanford Libraries CONDON ROLL 492","seeAlso":"https://purl.stanford.edu/pv279zy5193","exemplifies":{"catalogueNumber":"WM 1505","label":"Pückler, Graf Carl von (1857-1943): Sonata appassionata"},"keeper":{"name":"Stanford University Libraries","sameAs":[]},"conditions":[],"measurements":{"scanResolution":{"value":300.25,"unit":"px/in"},"holeSeparation":{"value":3.1959,"unit":"mm"}},"modifications":[{"@type":"Alteration","purpose":"control","produced":[{"@type":"Writing","@id":"copies/pv279zy5193.jsonld#inscription","technique":"handwriting","horizontal":{"unit":"mm","from":47250.18,"to":47429.18},"vertical":{"unit":"track","from":89,"to":103},"depiction":"https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/pv279zy5193%2Fpv279zy5193_0001/3470,558538,492,2116/full/90/default.jpg","transcription":{"@type":"text","@id":"copies/pv279zy5193.jsonld#inscription-text","text":"1505    28.  6.12   Hohn: / W[...]"}}],"actor":{"name":"Hohnrieder","sameAs":[],"@id":"hands.jsonld#hohnrieder","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/pv279zy5193.jsonld#hand-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/pv279zy5193.jsonld#hand-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"meaningComprehension","comprehends":["copies/pv279zy5193.jsonld#inscription-text"],"note":"Read as \"Hohn\". Countersigned by Wissler (https://pfefferniels.github.io/condon-dates/hands.jsonld#wissler); an act has one actor in linked-rolls, so the countersignature is stated here only."},{"@type":"inference","premises":[],"used":["https://pfefferniels.github.io/condon-dates/hands.jsonld"],"note":"The signature is clustered with the hand's other rolls by comparing the inscription images, not by the name read."}]}}}}],"scan":"https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/pv279zy5193%2Fpv279zy5193_0001/","readFrom":{"kind":"scan"},"production":{"company":{"name":"M. Welte & Söhne","sameAs":[]},"system":{"@id":"https://w3id.org/reo/type/system/welte-t100"},"date":{"within":"1912-06-28","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/pv279zy5193.jsonld#date-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/pv279zy5193.jsonld#date-belief","certainty":"true","reasons":[{"@type":"meaningComprehension","comprehends":["copies/pv279zy5193.jsonld#inscription-text"],"note":"crop 1, upper panel upright; ink, two lines. The month is the open-topped form that reading.md warns can be an 8, but the 8 in the day 28 on the same line is drawn with two closed bowls and looks nothing like it, so the month is a 6. The name beside the date is H-o-then three downstrokes: Hohn as written here, though the same strokes would also carry Holm, which German cursive does not distinguish. The second line is another name beginning with W, with a bar over its middle letters; I cannot resolve it and have not guessed."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/pv279zy5193.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":2.3958,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/pv279zy5193.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/pv279zy5193.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"AVG_HOLE_WIDTH of the roll's SUPRA analysis: the parser's box at its own grey level, averaged over every perforation it kept, so that a tear or a run of dust drags it. On the three copies measured both ways, an edge at half the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/p/pv279zy5193_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"chainPitch":{"value":3.0387,"unit":"mm","slot":2.4427,"bridge":0.5688,"n":352,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/pv279zy5193.jsonld#chain-pitch-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/pv279zy5193.jsonld#chain-pitch-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"Median over 352 pitches of held notes, measured on the IIIF image by punch-225/dates/pitch.py; slot and bridge are medians of their own.","used":["https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/pv279zy5193%2Fpv279zy5193_0001/","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"advance":{"value":1.014,"unit":"mm","strength":0.0755,"n":29854,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/pv279zy5193.jsonld#advance-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/pv279zy5193.jsonld#advance-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"The strongest period the 29854 slot lengths keep, by punch-225/advance.py (punch-225/dates/step.py); runners-up 0.446 mm at 0.0234, 0.537 mm at 0.032, 0.72 mm at 0.0517. The chain pitch is 2.997 of it. Held likely when found at a strength of at least 0.35 with the pitch within 0.15 of a whole number of it, possible when one of the two holds, unlikely when neither does.","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/p/pv279zy5193_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/step.py"]}]}}}}}}},{"@type":"RollCopy","@id":"copies/hj604wr7502.jsonld#copy"