 ||  2068"}}]}],"scan":"https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/zf673fy4620%2Fzf673fy4620_0001/","readFrom":{"kind":"scan"},"production":{"company":{"name":"M. Welte & Söhne","sameAs":[]},"system":{"@id":"https://w3id.org/reo/type/system/welte-t100"},"date":{"within":"1925-05-26","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/zf673fy4620.jsonld#date-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/zf673fy4620.jsonld#date-belief","certainty":"true","reasons":[{"@type":"meaningComprehension","comprehends":["copies/zf673fy4620.jsonld#inscription-text"],"note":"Stamped, not written. e1 carries five plain stamped figures, 26525, clear of the edge and whole, followed by a heavy over-inked mark. There is no blob before the figures, so the leading-mark trap does not apply here; the heavy mark falls after the last 5 and I cannot make out what it is, possibly a second slug. Read as day, month, two-figure year this is 26.5.25, and no other parse of five figures gives a possible date. The roll number is separate: a pencil 2068 at the edge in e2, matching the printed leader label in e4, 'WELTE-MIGNON. No. 2068 / Poeme / Op. 32, No. 1 / A. Scriabine / Played by A. Scriabine', which itself carries no date. e3 shows perforations only."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/zf673fy4620.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":1.7723,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/zf673fy4620.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/zf673fy4620.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"AVG_HOLE_WIDTH of the roll's SUPRA analysis: the parser's box at its own grey level, averaged over every perforation it kept, so that a tear or a run of dust drags it. On the three copies measured both ways, an edge at half the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/