t100"},"date":{"after":"1911-08-01","before":"1911-08-31","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/ph692rh6823.jsonld#date-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/ph692rh6823.jsonld#date-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"meaningComprehension","comprehends":["copies/ph692rh6823.jsonld#inscription-text"],"note":"two separate groups of four pencil figures on this roll, both in the same slanted hand just under the paper edge, neither with points or a name. Crop 2 reads 9811: the 8 and the two 1s are plain, the first figure is a closed loop over a descending tail, so 9, though a 2 is possible, which would give 2.8.11 instead of 9.8.11. Either way the month and year are August 1911, so only that much is entered. Crop 1 reads 4124, taken here as the roll number because 9811 cannot be one; but 4124 would also parse as 4.1.24, and nothing on the paper settles which of the two groups is the date. Crop 3 is the roll end and crop 4 holds only a crease and a smudge."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/ph692rh6823.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":1.6708,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/ph692rh6823.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/ph692rh6823.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"AVG_HOLE_WIDTH of the roll's SUPRA analysis: the parser's box at its own grey level, averaged over every perforation it kept, so that a tear or a run of dust drags it. On the three copies measured both ways, an edge at half the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/p/ph692rh6823_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"chainPitch":{"value":2.523,"unit":"mm","slot":1.7932,"bridge":0.7301,"n":321,"@a