 the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/f/fh358rd2268_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"chainPitch":{"value":2.6142,"unit":"mm","slot":1.8423,"bridge":0.762,"n":371,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/fh358rd2268.jsonld#chain-pitch-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/fh358rd2268.jsonld#chain-pitch-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"Median over 371 pitches of held notes, measured on the IIIF image by punch-225/dates/pitch.py; slot and bridge are medians of their own.","used":["https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/fh358rd2268%2Ffh358rd2268_0001/","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"advance":{"value":0.52,"unit":"mm","strength":0.6228,"n":29501,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/fh358rd2268.jsonld#advance-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/fh358rd2268.jsonld#advance-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"The strongest period the 29501 slot lengths keep, by punch-225/advance.py (punch-225/dates/step.py); runners-up 0.418 mm at 0.0729, 0.694 mm at 0.092. The chain pitch is 5.027 of it. Held likely when found at a strength of at least 0.35 with the pitch within 0.15 of a whole number of it, possible when one of the two holds, unlikely when neither does.","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/f/fh358rd2268_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/step.py"]}]}}}}}}},{"@type":"RollCopy","@id":"copies/kw738fg7467.jsonld#copy","label":"Condon Roll 669","identifier":"Stanford Libraries CONDON ROLL 669","seeAlso":"https://purl.stanford.edu/kw73