https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/wg598sj1504%2Fwg598sj1504_0001/3370,92882,720,2300/full/90/default.jpg","transcription":{"@type":"text","@id":"copies/wg598sj1504.jsonld#inscription-text","text":"4422"}}]}],"scan":"https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/wg598sj1504%2Fwg598sj1504_0001/","readFrom":{"kind":"scan"},"production":{"company":{"name":"M. Welte & Söhne","sameAs":[]},"system":{"@id":"https://w3id.org/reo/type/system/welte-t100"},"date":{"within":"1922-04-04","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/wg598sj1504.jsonld#date-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/wg598sj1504.jsonld#date-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"meaningComprehension","comprehends":["copies/wg598sj1504.jsonld#inscription-text"],"note":"Four figures in ink at the extreme paper edge, no separators, read as 4.4.22. The same hand writes the roll number 2621 further along the roll (crop e3), which gives a control on the figures: its 1 is a plain rising diagonal, while both opening figures here carry the crossbar of a 4, and its 2 is the curl with a horizontal foot that matches the last two figures here. Called medium rather than high because the strokes are thick at this resolution and 1 and 4 share a descender in this hand; if the two opening figures were 1s the reading would be 1.1.22, so the year 1922 holds either way. The printed label on the leader (e4) reads 'WELTE-MIGNON. No. 2621 / Etude Ges dur, Op. 10, No. 5 (Schwarze Tasten) / Fr. Chopin / Gespielt von Tosta di Benici', agreeing with the written number. Crop e2 holds a single figure 9 standing alone, the rest of whatever it belonged to falling outside the crop."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/wg598sj1504.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":1.7351,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/wg598sj1504.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/wg598sj1504.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","re