s":["copies/my670qk6863.jsonld#inscription-text"],"note":"stamped, not written, running across the roll; five figures of which the last three (4, 2, 5) are plain. The first figure carries the foot serif and top flag of a 1 but is only half inked, and the second shows a bottom bowl alone, so the day is left unread. Any sane split of the five figures leaves month 4 and year 25, hence 1925-04. The roll number 2673 is in pencil in crop 2 and on the printed label in crop 4 (WELTE-MIGNON No. 2673, Hymns, played by E. Adam). Crop 3 perforations only."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/my670qk6863.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":1.7841,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/my670qk6863.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/my670qk6863.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"AVG_HOLE_WIDTH of the roll's SUPRA analysis: the parser's box at its own grey level, averaged over every perforation it kept, so that a tear or a run of dust drags it. On the three copies measured both ways, an edge at half the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/m/my670qk6863_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"chainPitch":{"value":2.5174,"unit":"mm","slot":1.8849,"bridge":0.6344,"n":442,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/my670qk6863.jsonld#chain-pitch-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/my670qk6863.jsonld#chain-pitch-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"Median over 442 pitches of held notes, measured on the IIIF image by punch-225/dates/pitch.py; slot and bridge are medians of their own.","used":["https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/my670qk6863%2Fmy670qk6863_0001/","http