iif/jg717nb8731%2Fjg717nb8731_0001/","readFrom":{"kind":"scan"},"production":{"company":{"name":"M. Welte & Söhne","sameAs":[]},"system":{"@id":"https://w3id.org/reo/type/system/welte-t100"},"date":{"within":"1913-12-18","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/jg717nb8731.jsonld#date-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/jg717nb8731.jsonld#date-belief","certainty":"true","reasons":[{"@type":"meaningComprehension","comprehends":["copies/jg717nb8731.jsonld#inscription-text"],"note":"ink, two lines, plain in the upper panel of crop 1. The 8 in the day is the two-stroke form the instruction warns of, two strokes converging on one bottom bowl, but the 1 beside it and the 12 and 13 that follow leave the reading firm. The first figure of the number is a 2 with a looped top, settled by its horizontal base; the second is a 7 with a long descender. The name reads Wössler, though the vowel after the W is compressed and the umlaut is not distinct."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/jg717nb8731.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":2.2198,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/jg717nb8731.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/jg717nb8731.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"AVG_HOLE_WIDTH of the roll's SUPRA analysis: the parser's box at its own grey level, averaged over every perforation it kept, so that a tear or a run of dust drags it. On the three copies measured both ways, an edge at half the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/j/jg717nb8731_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"chainPitch":{"value":3.0127,"unit":"mm","slot":2.306,"bridge":0.6942,"n":315,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/jg717nb