nd I cannot make anything of it."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/fm197wc9522.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":1.7029,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/fm197wc9522.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/fm197wc9522.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"AVG_HOLE_WIDTH of the roll's SUPRA analysis: the parser's box at its own grey level, averaged over every perforation it kept, so that a tear or a run of dust drags it. On the three copies measured both ways, an edge at half the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/f/fm197wc9522_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"chainPitch":{"value":2.5049,"unit":"mm","slot":1.81,"bridge":0.7005,"n":337,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/fm197wc9522.jsonld#chain-pitch-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/fm197wc9522.jsonld#chain-pitch-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"Median over 337 pitches of held notes, measured on the IIIF image by punch-225/dates/pitch.py; slot and bridge are medians of their own.","used":["https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/fm197wc9522%2Ffm197wc9522_0001/","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"advance":{"value":0.5,"unit":"mm","strength":0.4593,"n":35564,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/fm197wc9522.jsonld#advance-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/fm197wc9522.jsonld#advance-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"The strongest period the 35564 slot lengths keep, by punch-225/advance.py (punch-225/dates/step.py); runners-up 0.87 mm at 0.0365,