e":"Pencil, treble edge, near the tail of the roll. Five figures, no separators, split 3 + 2 by spacing. The 1 is a plain caret, the 9 a closed bowl with a descender matching the 9 of the roll number, the 4 the looped form this hand uses in the number. The last figure is a closed double loop, both lobes inked on the left, so an 8 and not the open-left 3; if it were a 3 the year would be 23. Crop 1 holds only an ink blot; the roll number 2944 is written at the head of the roll (crop 3)."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/rg931dy5023.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":1.7765,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/rg931dy5023.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/rg931dy5023.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"AVG_HOLE_WIDTH of the roll's SUPRA analysis: the parser's box at its own grey level, averaged over every perforation it kept, so that a tear or a run of dust drags it. On the three copies measured both ways, an edge at half the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/r/rg931dy5023_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"chainPitch":{"value":2.5012,"unit":"mm","slot":1.9091,"bridge":0.5925,"n":382,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/rg931dy5023.jsonld#chain-pitch-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/rg931dy5023.jsonld#chain-pitch-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"Median over 382 pitches of held notes, measured on the IIIF image by punch-225/dates/pitch.py; slot and bridge are medians of their own.","used":["https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/rg931dy5023%2Frg931dy5023_0001/","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"advance":{"value":0.499,"unit":"mm","strength":0.4592,"n":39483,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/rg931dy5023.jsonld#advance-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/rg931dy5023.jsonld#advance-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"The strongest period the 39483 slot lengths keep, by punch-225/advance.py (punch-225/dates/step.py); runners-up 0.362 mm at 0.0254, 0.899 mm at 0.0433. The chain pitch is 5.012 of it. Held likely when found at a strength of at least 0.35 with the pitch within 0.15 of a whole number of it, possible when one of the two holds, unlikely when neither does.","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/r/rg931dy5023_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/step.py"]}]}}}}}}},{"@type":"RollCopy","@id":"copies/fb100cb2366.jsonld#copy","label":"Condon Roll 696","identifier":"Stanford Libraries CONDON ROLL 696","seeAlso":"https://purl.stanford.edu/fb100cb2366","exemplifies":{"catalogueNumber":"WM 2948","label":"Sommer, Ernst: Selections from \"Hansel & Gretel\""},"keeper":{"name":"Stanford University Libraries","sameAs":[]},"conditions":[],"measurements":{"scanResolution":{"value":300.25,"unit":"px/in"},"holeSeparation":{"value":3.2006,"unit":"mm"}},"modifications":[{"@type":"Alteration","purpose":"control","produced":[{"@type":"Writing","@id":"copies/fb100cb2366.jsonld#inscription","technique":"handwriting","horizontal":{"unit":"mm","from":37392.18,"to":37552.92},"vertical":{"unit":"track","from":90,"to":103},"depiction":"https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/fb100cb2366%2Ffb100cb2366_0001/3504,442008,460,1900/full/90/default.jpg","transcription":{"@type":"text","@id":"copies/fb100cb2366.jsonld#inscription-text","text":"27. 4. 17."},"medium":"pencil"}]}],"scan":"https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/fb100cb2366%2Ffb100cb2366_0001/","readFrom":{"kind":"scan"},"production":{"company":{"name":"M. Welte & Söhne","sameAs":[]},"system":{"@id":"https://w3id.org/reo/type/system/welte-t100"},"date":{"within":"1917-04-27","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/fb100cb2366.jsonld#date-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/fb100cb2366.jsonld#date-belief","certainty":"true","reasons":[{"@type":"meaningComprehension","comprehends":["copies/fb100cb2366.jsonld#inscription-text"],"note":"Pencil, treble edge, at the tail of the roll just past the last hole. Both 7s are the barred continental form (upstroke, long diagonal down-left, crossbar); the 1 before the second 7 is a plain caret with no crossbar, so 17 and not 11 or 77. The 4 is the open-top form. The crop clips the very tops of the figures at the panel edge, but the crossbars and diagonals are complete. The roll number 2948. is written separately at the head of the roll (region 2), in what looks like the same hand; its last figure is the open-loop form that can read as 6. Region 4, on the leader, carries a later note in English cursive about the roll's condition (\"... especially bass + treble ... over the ... election. ... bite -\"), a different and later hand with no date. Region 3 is a stain."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/fb100cb2366.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":1.7511,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/fb100cb2366.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/fb100cb2366.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"AVG_HOLE_WIDTH of the roll's SUPRA analysis: the parser's box at its own grey level, averaged over every perforation it kept, so that a tear or a run of dust drags it. On the three copies measured both ways, an edge at half the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analy