q268fs9721.jsonld#inscription-text"],"note":"Pencil, treble edge, at the tail of the roll. Five figures, very faint and cut along their tops by the crop edge. The last is the barred 7 of these hands and the one before it a 2, giving the year 27; the middle figure matches the 5 of the roll number written at the head of the roll (crop 3), giving May; the fourth-from-last is a 2, so the day ends in 2, but its first figure is illegible and I have not guessed it. Crop 4 shows the printed leader label, WELTE-MIGNON No. 3045, Debussy Preludes, M. Welte & Soehne Freiburg i. B., with a signature in the \"Played by\" box; it carries no date. Crop 2 is a damp stain."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/tq268fs9721.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":1.7503,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/tq268fs9721.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/tq268fs9721.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"AVG_HOLE_WIDTH of the roll's SUPRA analysis: the parser's box at its own grey level, averaged over every perforation it kept, so that a tear or a run of dust drags it. On the three copies measured both ways, an edge at half the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/t/tq268fs9721_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"chainPitch":{"value":2.5058,"unit":"mm","slot":1.8798,"bridge":0.6299,"n":464,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/tq268fs9721.jsonld#chain-pitch-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/tq268fs9721.jsonld#chain-pitch-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"Median over 464 pitches of held notes, measured on the IIIF image by punch-225/dates/pitch.py; slot and bridge