mprehends":["copies/jd143sb1087.jsonld#inscription-text"],"note":"stamped, and preceded by the heavy fixed mark of the slug, which I have not counted as a figure: the figures alone give a possible date, so the mark is the same blob reading.md warns about. Every figure is plain in both panels. e4 carries a separate four-figure number in ink, 5553 or 6553, with the tops of the figures along the crop edge; e1 is torn, e2 and e5 hold nothing but the leader tab and the colour target"}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/jd143sb1087.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":1.686,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/jd143sb1087.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/jd143sb1087.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"AVG_HOLE_WIDTH of the roll's SUPRA analysis: the parser's box at its own grey level, averaged over every perforation it kept, so that a tear or a run of dust drags it. On the three copies measured both ways, an edge at half the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/j/jd143sb1087_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"chainPitch":{"value":2.5964,"unit":"mm","slot":1.8253,"bridge":0.7597,"n":43,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/jd143sb1087.jsonld#chain-pitch-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/jd143sb1087.jsonld#chain-pitch-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"Median over 43 pitches of held notes, measured on the IIIF image by punch-225/dates/pitch.py; slot and bridge are medians of their own.","used":["https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/jd143sb1087%2Fjd143sb1087_0001/","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049