 7309 slot lengths keep, by punch-225/advance.py (punch-225/dates/step.py); runners-up 0.399 mm at 0.0929, 0.635 mm at 0.1118. The chain pitch is 5.053 of it. Held likely when found at a strength of at least 0.35 with the pitch within 0.15 of a whole number of it, possible when one of the two holds, unlikely when neither does.","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/y/ys250pr2232_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/step.py"]}]}}}}}}},{"@type":"RollCopy","@id":"copies/yk645sm6970.jsonld#copy","label":"Condon Roll 915","identifier":"Stanford Libraries CONDON ROLL 915","seeAlso":"https://purl.stanford.edu/yk645sm6970","exemplifies":{"catalogueNumber":"WM 5905","label":"Sommer, Hans (1904-2000): Hallelujah! : fox-trot from \"Hit the deck\""},"keeper":{"name":"Stanford University Libraries","sameAs":[]},"conditions":[],"measurements":{"scanResolution":{"value":300.25,"unit":"px/in"},"holeSeparation":{"value":3.1916,"unit":"mm"}},"modifications":[{"@type":"Alteration","purpose":"control","produced":[{"@type":"Writing","@id":"copies/yk645sm6970.jsonld#inscription","technique":"handwriting","horizontal":{"unit":"mm","from":13838.41,"to":13999.14},"vertical":{"unit":"track","from":70,"to":84},"depiction":"https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/yk645sm6970%2Fyk645sm6970_0001/2766,163582,516,1900/full/270/default.jpg","transcription":{"@type":"text","@id":"copies/yk645sm6970.jsonld#inscription-text","text":"[stamped mark] 18128"}}]}],"scan":"https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/yk645sm6970%2Fyk645sm6970_0001/","readFrom":{"kind":"scan"},"production":{"company":{"name":"M. Welte & Söhne","sameAs":[]},"system":{"@id":"https://w3id.org/reo/type/system/welte-t100"},"date":{"within":"1928-01-18","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/yk645sm6970.jsonld#date-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/yk645sm6970.jsonld#date-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"meaningComprehension","comprehends":["copies/yk645sm6970.jsonld#inscription-text"],"note":"stamped, running down the roll at about sixty degrees, upright in the lower panel after rotation. A heavily inked mark, a vertical with two bars projecting to the right and a detached blob below it, stands before five plain figures, 1 8 1 2 8. The same mark, down to the detached blob, precedes the figures on rd899zb5188 and jd143sb1087 in batch 32, and on none of the three can it be read as a figure without destroying the date, so I take it for a fixed slug rather than a digit. Five figures with the leading zeros dropped give 18.1.28. Later than the 1904-1926 span reading.md reports, as is md908xy8241."}]}}},"perforator":{"@type":"Perforator","@id":"copies/yk645sm6970.jsonld#perforator","condition":{"conditionType":"setting","punchDiameter":{"value":1.7824,"unit":"mm","@annotation":{"@id":"copies/yk645sm6970.jsonld#punch-diameter-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/yk645sm6970.jsonld#punch-diameter-belief","certainty":"possible","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"AVG_HOLE_WIDTH of the roll's SUPRA analysis: the parser's box at its own grey level, averaged over every perforation it kept, so that a tear or a run of dust drags it. On the three copies measured both ways, an edge at half the contrast put the punch 0.10 to 0.15 mm wider (punch-225/README.md).","used":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pianoroll/piano-roll-analyses/main/analysis/y/yk645sm6970_analysis.txt.bz2","https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/pitch.py"]}]}}},"chainPitch":{"value":2.5936,"unit":"mm","slot":1.9032,"bridge":0.6831,"n":229,"@annotation":{"@id":"copies/yk645sm6970.jsonld#chain-pitch-annotation","belief":{"@type":"belief","@id":"copies/yk645sm6970.jsonld#chain-pitch-belief","certainty":"likely","reasons":[{"@type":"measurement","note":"Median over 229 pitches of held notes, measu